# 🔍 WanderLust — Complete Architectural & Product Analysis

---

## STEP 1 — PROJECT UNDERSTANDING

### 1. What Problem This Project Solves

WanderLust is an **Airbnb clone** — a vacation rental marketplace where:
- **Hosts** can list properties (with images, pricing, location, maps)
- **Guests** can browse listings, read reviews, and leave reviews
- The app provides **map-based location discovery** via Mapbox

It solves the core problem of connecting property owners with travelers seeking accommodation.

### 2. Current Product Flow (User Journey)

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Landing → /listings] --> B[Browse All Listings Grid]
    B --> C[Click Listing → /listings/:id]
    C --> D{Logged In?}
    D -->|No| E[View Only - No Actions]
    D -->|Yes| F[Leave Review]
    D -->|Yes & Owner| G[Edit / Delete Listing]
    
    H[Signup → /signup] --> I[Auto Login → /listings]
    J[Login → /login] --> K[Redirect to saved URL or /listings]
    
    L[Create Listing → /listings/new] --> M{Logged In?}
    M -->|No| J
    M -->|Yes| N[Fill Form + Upload Image → Geocode → Save]
```

**User Journey Summary:**
1. Anonymous user lands on `/` → redirected to `/listings`
2. Browses card grid of all listings (no filtering actually works)
3. Clicks a listing → sees details, map, reviews
4. Must sign up/login to create listings or leave reviews
5. Owner can edit/delete their own listings
6. Any logged-in user can review any listing (including their own)
7. Review author or listing owner can delete reviews

### 3. How Frontend, Backend & DB Interact

```mermaid
graph LR
    Browser["Browser (EJS + Bootstrap)"] -->|"Form POST / GET"| Express["Express Server"]
    Express -->|"Mongoose ODM"| MongoDB["MongoDB Atlas"]
    Express -->|"Multer Upload"| Cloudinary["Cloudinary CDN"]
    Express -->|"Forward Geocode"| Mapbox["Mapbox API"]
    Browser -->|"Client-side Map"| MapboxGL["Mapbox GL JS"]
```

| Layer | Technology | Role |
|-------|-----------|------|
| **Frontend** | EJS + Bootstrap 5 + Vanilla JS | Server-rendered HTML, no SPA |
| **Backend** | Express.js 4.x | HTTP routing, auth, business logic |
| **Database** | MongoDB Atlas via Mongoose 8.x | Document storage |
| **Auth** | Passport.js + passport-local-mongoose | Session-based auth |
| **File Upload** | Multer + Cloudinary | Image storage |
| **Maps** | Mapbox SDK (server) + Mapbox GL JS (client) | Geocoding + map display |
| **Sessions** | express-session + connect-mongo | Server-side sessions in MongoDB |
| **Validation** | Joi | Request body validation |

### 4. Current Architecture Pattern

**Hybrid MVC (Route-Controller-Model)** — a standard Express pattern:

```
Routes → Middleware → Controllers → Models → MongoDB
                                  → External APIs (Mapbox, Cloudinary)
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> There is **no service layer**. Controllers directly call Mongoose models and external APIs. This is acceptable for a small project but becomes a problem at scale.

### 5. Strengths of Current Implementation

| Strength | Details |
|----------|---------|
| ✅ Clean MVC separation | Routes, controllers, models are properly separated files |
| ✅ Joi validation | Server-side input validation exists for listings and reviews |
| ✅ Middleware pattern | Auth ([isLoggedIn](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/Projects/wanderLust/middleware.js#6-15)), authorization ([isOwner](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/Projects/wanderLust/middleware.js#24-33), [isReviewAuthor](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/Projects/wanderLust/middleware.js#34-43)), validation are proper middleware |
| ✅ Error handling | [wrapAsync](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/Projects/wanderLust/utils/wrapAsync.js#1-6) + [ExpressError](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/Projects/wanderLust/utils/ExpressError.js#1-8) + global error handler is a good pattern |
| ✅ Cloudinary integration | Image uploads to CDN rather than local filesystem |
| ✅ GeoJSON + Mapbox | Proper geospatial data storage with interactive maps |
| ✅ Session store in MongoDB | Sessions use `connect-mongo` — production-appropriate vs. in-memory |
| ✅ Flash messages | User feedback via `connect-flash` works well |
| ✅ Post-delete cleanup | `findOneAndDelete` hook cascades review deletions — good data integrity |
| ✅ Redirect URL saved | Login redirect preserves user's intended destination |

### 6. Weak Points / Technical Debt

| Category | Issue | Severity |
|----------|-------|----------|
| 🔴 **CRITICAL** | [.env](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/Projects/wanderLust/.env) committed to Git with **real credentials** (MongoDB password, Cloudinary API key, Mapbox token, session secret) | **P0** |
| 🔴 **CRITICAL** | Session secret is `"mysecretcode"` — trivially guessable | **P0** |
| 🔴 **CRITICAL** | No CSRF protection on any form | **P0** |
| 🔴 **CRITICAL** | `CLOUD_API_SECRET` is referenced in code but **missing from .env** — uploads may silently fail | **P1** |
| 🟡 **Major** | `Listing.find({})` loads **all listings** into memory — no pagination | **P1** |
| 🟡 **Major** | Filter UI is purely decorative — clicking filters does nothing | **P1** |
| 🟡 **Major** | Search bar is non-functional — form submits to `GET` with no backend handler | **P1** |
| 🟡 **Major** | Seed data has **copy-paste coordinates** — most listings point to Serengeti regardless of location | **P2** |
| 🟡 **Major** | No rate limiting anywhere — vulnerable to brute-force and spam | **P2** |
| 🟠 **Medium** | `app.listen()` is called **before** routes are mounted (line 83 vs 95) | **P2** |
| 🟠 **Medium** | Flash message middleware is **after** session init but **before** routes — ordering is fragile | **P2** |
| 🟠 **Medium** | Typo: `fallowedFormats` in cloudConfig should be `allowedFormats` | **P2** |
| 🟠 **Medium** | Footer links (`/privacy`, `/terms`, `/details`) lead to 404 — no routes exist | **P3** |
| 🟠 **Medium** | No test suite whatsoever — [package.json](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/Projects/wanderLust/package.json) test script echoes an error | **P3** |
| 🟢 **Minor** | Razorpay is in [package.json](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/Projects/wanderLust/package.json) but never used in code | **P3** |
| 🟢 **Minor** | `cookie-parser` is in dependencies but never imported | **P3** |
| 🟢 **Minor** | `console.log(req.body)` in review controller — debug logging in production | **P3** |

