## STEP 3 — PRODUCTION READINESS REVIEW

### Is This Project Ready For…

| Criterion | Ready? | Blockers |
|-----------|--------|----------|
| **Real Users** | 🔴 No | Exposed credentials, no CSRF, no email verification, broken search/filters |
| **High Traffic** | 🔴 No | No pagination, no caching, no CDN for static assets, no load balancing |
| **Large Database** | 🔴 No | No indexes, `find({})` all docs, unbounded review arrays, no pagination |
| **Multiple Developers** | 🟡 Partially | Clean file structure helps, but no tests, no linting, no CI/CD, no Docker |
| **Future Features** | 🟡 Partially | MVC helps extensibility, but no service layer, no booking system, no search |

### Top 10 Production Blockers (Ranked)

1. **🔴 Leaked credentials in [.env](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Desktop/Projects/wanderLust/.env)** — Rotate ALL secrets immediately
2. **🔴 No CSRF protection** — Any site can forge actions on behalf of logged-in users
3. **🔴 No pagination** — Server will crash under load
4. **🔴 Weak session secret** — Sessions can be forged
5. **🟡 No security headers** (Helmet) — XSS, clickjacking, MIME sniffing risks
6. **🟡 No rate limiting** — Brute-force attacks, spam possible
7. **🟡 No test suite** — Can't safely refactor or deploy
8. **🟡 No input sanitization** — Potential NoSQL injection via `req.body`
9. **🟡 Broken features** — Search and filters are fake UI
10. **🟡 No booking system** — The core business feature doesn't exist

